  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Madaba \u2192 Philadelpheia;\u00a0Philadelpheia \u2192 Map 69; Madaba \u2192 Petra;\u00a0Betthorus \u2192 Castra Mefaa \u2192 Philadelpheia; Da'janiya \u2192 Dhat Ras;\u00a0Esbous \u2192 Livias \u2192 Hierichous;\u00a0Mortuum Mare \u2192 Via Nova Traiana; Mothous \u2192 Arindela;\u00a0Petra region;\u00a0Philadelpheia \u2192 Gerasa (Map 69).\u00a0<span>For\u00a0</span><em>Barrington Atlas</em><span>\u00a0map 69,\u00a0</span>Adra(h)a \u2192 Kapitolias;\u00a0Adra(h)a \u2192 Gerasa \u2192 S;\u00a0Ake \u2192 Bethsaida \u2192 Kochaba;\u00a0Ake \u2192 Legio \u2192 Ginai(a) \u2192 Samaria \u2192\u00a0Khirbet et Tira;\u00a0Ake \u2192 Sepphoris;\u00a0Apollonia \u2192 SE;\u00a0Berytus \u2192 Heliopolis;\u00a0Bostra \u2192 Adra(h)a;\u00a0Bostra \u2192 Gerasa;\u00a0Bostra \u2192 Nelkomia;\u00a0Bostra \u2192 Triacome \u2192 Mothana \u2192 S;\u00a0Buraq \u2192 Dionysias;\u00a0Caesarea \u2192 Gaba Philippi;\u00a0Caesarea \u2192 Kapharsaba \u2192 Antipatris (Map\u00a070); Caesarea \u2192 Legio \u2192 Scythopolis;\u00a0Caesarea \u2192 Neapolis \u2192 Korea(i);\u00a0Caesarea \u2192 Scythopolis via Ginai(a);\u00a0coast road;\u00a0Damascus \u2192 Casama;\u00a0Dionysias \u2192 Canatha \u2192 Nelkomia;\u00a0Dionysias \u2192 Salamanestha; el-Ghassule;\u00a0Gadara \u2192 Pella \u2192 Asophon \u2192 S;\u00a0Gadara \u2192 Scythopolis;\u00a0Gadara \u2192 Tiberias;\u00a0Heliopolis \u2192 Damascus;\u00a0Heliopolis \u2192 N;\u00a0Khan el-Abyad \u2192 Thelseae \u2192 Damascus \u2192\u00a0Aere \u2192 Neue \u2192 S;\u00a0Nejha;\u00a0Palaibyblos \u2192 Sidon \u2192 Caesarea \u2192\u00a0Apollonia;\u00a0Paneas \u2192 Bethsaida; Phaine \u2192 *Airita \u2192 Dionysias \u2192 Bostra;\u00a0S \u2192 Gerasa \u2192 Pella \u2192 Scythopolis; Tiberias \u2192 Bethsaida \u2192 Hippos \u2192 Sennabris\u00a0Tiberias \u2192 Sepphoris \u2192 Legio;\u00a0Tricomia \u2192 Umm al-Quttein \u2192 S;\u00a0Tyrus \u2192 Paneas \u2192 Damascus;\u00a0Via Nova Traiana \u2192 Umm al-Jimal</p>\r\n<p>The Via Nova Traiana is marked on two maps in the Barrington Atlas, namely\u00a069 D5 and 71 B2.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Via Nova Traiana is a Roman road built along the Limes Arabicus during the reigns of the emperors Trajan and Hadrian. The route may supersede an earlier one known as the \"Via Regia\" or \"King's Highway\", a route of communication and transhumance in use since the Neolithic period.",
